// strip_json_fence.dg — Claude sometimes wraps its JSON output in a markdown code fence
// ("```json\n{...}\n```") even when the prompt asks for "ONLY a JSON object, with no surrounding
// text" — confirmed live: this broke `writtenText.toMap()` in every digest_finish_<profile>.dg
// with "Invalid JSON Format String", since the fence markers aren't valid JSON.
//
// A regex-based strip (leading ```<lang>\n? / trailing ```\s*) was tried first but did nothing
// live (cleaned text came back the exact same length as the input) — Deluge's regex engine has
// already proven surprising more than once this session (e.g. rejecting an escaped "{" as
// invalid), so this avoids regex entirely: find the first "{" and the last "}" and extract
// exactly that substring. Robust to whatever surrounds the real JSON (fence markers, language
// tags, whitespace) regardless of exact formatting. Safe to call unconditionally — if the text is
// already fence-free JSON, this still finds the same first "{"/last "}" and returns equivalent
// content (modulo any leading/trailing whitespace, already trimmed).

string standalone.stripJsonFence(String text)
{
	cleaned = text.trim();
	startIdx = cleaned.indexOf("{");
	endIdx = cleaned.lastIndexOf("}");
	if (startIdx >= 0 && endIdx > startIdx) {
		cleaned = cleaned.subText(startIdx, endIdx + 1);
	}
	return cleaned.trim();
}
